            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10. Both Rutherford’s and Bohr’s models have electrons orbiting the nucleus. Why did Rutherford’s model fail to explain atomic stability, while Bohr’s model succeeded?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.227,
            0.142,
            0.889,
