        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.227,
            0.643,
            0.889,
            0.711
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "15. In an atom, there are 12 protons and 12 neutrons in the nucleus. Now, imagine that all the electrons are replaced with some hypothetical particles that have the same charge as electrons but are 500 times heavier. What effect will this replacement have on the atom’s:"
